{"symbol":"BRCA1","resolved":{"input":"BRCA1","symbol":"BRCA1","ncbi_gene_id":"672","name":"BRCA1 DNA repair associated","location":"17q21.31","aliases":["BRCAI","BRCC1","BROVCA1","FANCS","IRIS","PNCA4","PPP1R53","PSCP","RNF53"],"uniprot":"P38398","uniprot_reviewed":true},"function":[{"text":"BRCA1 function (UniProt P38398, UniProt evidence code ECO:0000269): E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase that specifically mediates the formation of 'Lys-6'-linked polyubiquitin chains and plays a central role in DNA repair by facilitating cellular responses to DNA damage. It is unclear whether it also mediates the formation of other types of polyubiquitin chains. The BRCA1-BARD1 heterodimer coordinates a diverse range of cellular pathways such as DNA damage repair, ubiquitination and transcriptional regulation to maintain genomic stability. Regulates centrosomal microtubule nucleation. Required for appropriate cell cycle arrests after ionizing irradiation in both the S-phase and the G2 phase of the cell cycle. Required for FANCD2 targeting to sites of DNA damage. ...","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"P38398","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P38398/entry","title":"BRCA1: Breast cancer type 1 susceptibility protein"},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:10500182","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10500182/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:10724175","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10724175/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:11836499","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11836499/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:12183412","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12183412/","title":""}]}],"go":[{"text":"BRCA1 GO biological process annotations: cellular response to indole-3-methanol, cellular response to ionizing radiation, cellular response to tumor necrosis factor, chromosome segregation, DNA damage tolerance, double-strand break repair, double-strand break repair via homologous recombinatio